2026-09-23T07:02:37.4999303Z     The ``pytest`` framework makes it easy to write small tests, yet
2026-09-23T07:02:37.4999537Z     scales to support complex functional testing for applications and libraries.
2026-09-23T07:02:37.4999612Z     
2026-09-23T07:02:37.4999715Z     An example of a simple test:
2026-09-23T07:02:37.4999794Z     
2026-09-23T07:02:37.4999892Z     .. code-block:: python
2026-09-23T07:02:37.4999965Z     
2026-09-23T07:02:37.5000071Z         # content of test_sample.py
2026-09-23T07:02:37.5000156Z         def inc(x):
2026-09-23T07:02:37.5000245Z             return x + 1
2026-09-23T07:02:37.5000323Z     
2026-09-23T07:02:37.5000398Z     
2026-09-23T07:02:37.5000491Z         def test_answer():
2026-09-23T07:02:37.5000584Z             assert inc(3) == 5
2026-09-23T07:02:37.5000660Z     
2026-09-23T07:02:37.5000733Z     
2026-09-23T07:02:37.5000824Z     To execute it::
2026-09-23T07:02:37.5000900Z     
2026-09-23T07:02:37.5000985Z         $ pytest
2026-09-23T07:02:37.5001142Z         ============================= test session starts =============================
2026-09-23T07:02:37.5001236Z         collected 1 items
2026-09-23T07:02:37.5001313Z     
2026-09-23T07:02:37.5001407Z         test_sample.py F
2026-09-23T07:02:37.5001485Z     
2026-09-23T07:02:37.5001629Z         ================================== FAILURES ===================================
2026-09-23T07:02:37.5001799Z         _________________________________ test_answer _________________________________
2026-09-23T07:02:37.5001873Z     
2026-09-23T07:02:37.5001968Z             def test_answer():
2026-09-23T07:02:37.5002064Z         >       assert inc(3) == 5
2026-09-23T07:02:37.5002154Z         E       assert 4 == 5
2026-09-23T07:02:37.5002254Z         E        +  where 4 = inc(3)
2026-09-23T07:02:37.5002331Z     
2026-09-23T07:02:37.5002440Z         test_sample.py:5: AssertionError
2026-09-23T07:02:37.5002595Z         ========================== 1 failed in 0.04 seconds ===========================
2026-09-23T07:02:37.5002672Z     
2026-09-23T07:02:37.5002750Z     
2026-09-23T07:02:37.5003599Z     Thanks to ``pytest``'s detailed assertion introspection, you can simply use plain ``assert`` statements. See `getting-started <https://docs.pytest.org/en/stable/getting-started.html#our-first-test-run>`_ for more examples.
